From 87ac40ac760c9b7e21214fb1323185b0f322efc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:13:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: verisilicon: add a stateful RK3399 H.264 encoder

Expose a separate V4L2 encoder node for Annex B Constrained Baseline
streams. VEPU2 emits the slices. The driver writes SPS and PPS in
software with source colorimetry and frame timing.

Return queued buffers on stream start failure. Complete failed jobs
and media requests in the Hantro core, including VP9 and AV1
preparation errors. Resume encoding when OUTPUT restarts after a
drain. Refresh stream headers after source format changes.

Link: https://github.com/bootlin/linux/blob/eacf5601e410d89e4ec214193b273262afec4dba/drivers/staging/media/hantro/rk3399_vpu_hw_h264_enc.c
Link: https://github.com/bootlin/v4l2-hantro-h264-encoder/blob/5df9d09b5ab5decdb6b66b0f6bf8daababfa9ba2/h264.c
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/20260522101653.2565125-13-paulk@sys-base.io/
Link: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel/+/refs/heads/chromeos-5.10/drivers/staging/media/hantro/rk3399_vpu_hw_h264_enc.c
